  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is very strong: all thermal incidents reported to the regulator within 24 hours, customers notified within 48 hours, with no confirmed-cause-only or serious-only limitation. S2 keeps the 55 °C test and a hard 5% limit with per-model numeric results given to purchasers and regulators but not published publicly, satisfying both NW-1 and HC-1; the weak point is that above-limit sales can continue under regulator-set deadlines with no fixed remediation cap, though the regulator must suspend sales if noncompliance persists. S3 lets new units wait 24 months and allows a 6-year 'where feasible' retrofit with an alternative-measure escape, while S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months and S5 retains an explicit mandatory 8-per-100,000 model-specific recall with no transition, plus only a 'promptly' customer-notice standard."
 },
